## Useful pointers

- **`WIKI_SCHEMA.md`** — vault_id, layout, conventions, promotion rules.
- **`00-Vault-Index/index.md`** — read-only catalog (auto-generated).
- **`00-Vault-Index/log/`** — monthly append-only journal.
- **obsidian-llm-wiki** — the index layer (17 CLIs). Search/RAG: `/wiki-search`
  (incl. `--tag <class>` + temporal `--as-of <date>`), `/wiki-query`, `/wiki-verify-multi`.
  Construction: **`/wiki-import`** (the unified construct path — URL/PDF/office/thread/
  transcript/local file, any layout via config, ADR-007), `/wiki-extract-concepts`,
  `/wiki-sync` (mixed-zone driver), `/wiki-append-log`.
  Entity & event graph: `/wiki-confirm`, `/wiki-alias`,
  `/wiki-merge`, `/wiki-graph` (typed page-to-page edges — implements/supersedes/causes/
  invalidated_by/uses/owns/…, authored one direction, inverse auto-derived). Lifecycle/health:
  `/wiki-init`, `/wiki-reindex`, `/wiki-index-upsert`, `/wiki-index-render`,
  `/wiki-lint`, `/wiki-health`. Install per its `README.md`; ensure its `bin/` is on `PATH`.
- **obsidian-cli** — the skill that drives the *running* Obsidian app via its official
  CLI (Obsidian 1.12+): link-safe `rename`/`move` (the app rewrites backlinks — a plain
  `mv` orphans them), typed properties, tasks, daily notes, Bases queries, history
  restore. **Active-note resolution:** say *"edit the note"* / *"the note about X"* with
  **no path** → run `obsidian-active-note focused` / `match --descriptor "X"` **bare from this
  vault's terminal** (it auto-detects the vault from the CWD — no `--vault` needed) to resolve
  your **active/open tab** — a descriptor matching one open note = exact hit (no ask), a bare
  "the note" = confirm once per session, not-found/ambiguous = it asks. **Need a folder, not a
  file** (e.g. to hand `/wiki-sync <zone>` the current folder without copying a path)?
  `obsidian-active-note folder` derives the open note's containing folder (`--descriptor "X"` →
  a named note's folder); a folder is a **folder-WIDE** blast radius, so echo `folder ← note` and
  confirm before the folder-wide op (a root note scopes the WHOLE vault). It routes knowledge lookups to
  `/wiki-search` first and, after any app-side mutation of this (registered) vault,
  refreshes the index **in the same turn** (`wiki-index-upsert` after a content edit;
  **`wiki-reindex --delta` after a rename/move** — rename-aware since TASK 030; `--full` =
  fallback/swap remedy). T3 (`eval`/`dev:*`) is banned by default — never from note content.
